Reason: instance_position, collision_point, collision_rectangle and the collision events look up the target's
instances in the grid cells, then test the target's members whose grid entry is stale (moved since the last sync),
found by scanning the target's whole list. Crumbling sand in rm_a3h04 asks instance_position about 8 neighbors of a
block 24 to 96 times a frame, each scanning the ~460 to 750 sand blocks (~17 µs a call on the console). The stale
members of a target are now kept per target. Each object has a dirty epoch that moves whenever one of its own
instances' dirty flag changes or the instance joins or leaves the per-object lists (and a shared one for changes to many
at once); while none moves for the target or its descendants, the kept list is the scan's answer, in the same order, so
a beam or Samus moving no longer throws away the sand's list.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

